#. While a toxin is waiting and no slot is chosen: tapping a slot round the
#. body (outside) makes it venom, the slot in the body (inside) makes it
#. poison.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 271 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap a slot · venom outside, poison inside"
msgstr ""

#. When the player tries to put a gene other than a toxin into the slot inside
#. the body: only a toxin works there. %s is the gene's short word, such as
#. `swim`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 178 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s works only outside"
msgstr ""

#. A slot is chosen for a waiting toxin; a second tap places it, as the form
#. it takes in that slot. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 205 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to place %s here"
msgstr ""

#. A slot is chosen for a waiting toxin, but the toxin would become a form the
#. cell already carries, so a second tap adds one copy of it where it already
#. is. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 225 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to add a copy to %s"
msgstr ""

#. As above, but that form already has the most copies a gene can have, three,
#. so placing it there would do nothing. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 215 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s has three copies already"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a waiting toxin over a slot where it would add a copy to a
#. form the cell already carries: letting go chooses the slot, and a second
#. tap adds the copy. %s is `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 305 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go, then tap again to add a copy to %s"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene to a slot where it would turn into a form the cell
#. already carries (venom outside, poison inside), which is not allowed. %s is
#. `venom` or `poison`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 366 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "here it would become %s, which you already carry"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a toxin into a slot of the other place: letting go moves it
#. there, and it changes form. The first %s is its word now, the second the
#. word it becomes, such as "let go to move venom here · it becomes poison".
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 315 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to move %s here · it becomes %s"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene onto another, where the swap moves one of them
#. between outside and inside and changes its form. The first two %s are the
#. two genes' words; the last two say which one changes and what it becomes.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word,
#. your second widest, your second widest and your second widest in place of
#. the placeholders; the English takes 382 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s · %s becomes %s"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging venom onto poison (or the reverse): the two swap places and
#. change forms, so in effect they trade copies. The two %s are the two words.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 351 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s · they trade copies"
msgstr ""

